  "key_findings": [
    "SPY vol → GLD vol Granger causality: YES",
    "SPY vol → TLT vol Granger causality: YES",
    "VIX → GLD vol Granger causality: YES",
    "Spillover VT Sharpe improvement: -0.0781",
    "DM test p-value: 0.0385"
  ],
  "conclusion": "SPY vol Granger-causes GLD vol (F=5.33, p=0.005) and TLT vol (F=35.26, p<0.001) — equity stress statistically propagates to gold and bond volatility. However, this is regime-dependent: spillover only significant in HIGH vol regimes (SPY→GLD: F=6.55, p=0.001) but NOT in low/mid vol regimes. VIX is a stronger universal predictor (F=19-265). Cross-correlation is predominantly contemporaneous (lag 0), limiting predictive value. Practically, vol spillover does NOT improve portfolio VT — spillover-informed VT has LOWER Sharpe (1.81 vs 1.89, DM t=-2.07, p=0.039). Asset-specific VT is sufficient; cross-asset vol information adds no incremental portfolio value. This reinforces K41: VT's value is mechanical (insurance), not informational."
}